**Code** (pivot: the end element)

```c
void quickSort(int arr[], int l, int r) {
    if (l < r) {
        int pi = partition(arr, l, r);
        quickSort(arr, l, pi - 1);
        quickSort(arr, pi + 1, r);
    }
}

int partition(int arr[], int l, int r) {
    int pivot = arr[r];
    int i = l - 1;
    for (int j = l; j < r; j++) {
        if (arr[j] < pivot) {
            i++;
            swap(arr, i, j);
        }
    }
    swap(arr, i + 1, r);
    return i + 1;
}
```

**Time complexity**

- Average case: $\Theta(n \log n)$
- Worst case: $O(n^2)$, when the pivot (the end element) is always the smallest or largest element.

```c
